# Dispatcher harness

`crew`, `dispatch` and `dispatcher` are on your PATH.

- `dispatcher` promotes a session into an orchestrator: it judges each task into
  tier + engine + model + effort, scaffolds one worker per task via `dispatch`,
  and watches the `crew` bus. A dispatcher never implements, gates, or opens PRs.
- A dispatched worker reads `WORKER_PROTOCOL.md` and runs its task end-to-end.
  `dispatch` passes that path to the worker on the command line, so a worker
  never has to resolve it. To read it yourself, use
  `$DISPATCHER_PROTOCOL_DIR/WORKER_PROTOCOL.md` when that variable is set.
- Cursor workers skip the plan-critic and code-review gates (Claude-only) but
  still delegate execute subagents per `WORKER_PROTOCOL.md` rule 1. Emit
  `plan_critic_first_pass: null`, `review_high: null`, `review_mode: "none"` —
  ungated, not unorchestrated.

Run `crew` with no arguments for the full subcommand surface.
